<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tianjin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tientsin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tianjin is a major port city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, about 120 km south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> near the Bohai Sea. After the Treaties of Tianjin of 1858 and the Convention of Peking of 1860 it became a treaty port, with concessions held by several foreign powers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> occupied it in July 1937 at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a>, and it is now one of China's municipalities under direct central government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tianjin.jpg" alt="Tianjin" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KangTyngrwey · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tianjin_Eye_and_Tianjin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
